**Diagnosis**

Observed source-level bug: `assets/compact-buy.js` uses `document.querySelector`, so it binds only the first `[data-variant-select]` and first `[data-cart-variant]` on the page. With two `compact-buy` sections, the second selector has no listener and its own hidden `name="id"` input is never updated.

A second bug is lifecycle-related: the listener is only attached on `DOMContentLoaded`. When the Theme Editor replaces/re-renders a section after initial load, the new selector is inserted after that event and is not initialized.

**Smallest Compatible Patch**

Scope: `sections/compact-buy.liquid` and `assets/compact-buy.js` only. Preserve the standard cart add route, translations, variant availability logic, and merchant settings. No upload or publish.

Recommended patch:

```liquid
<div data-product-picker data-section-id="{{ section.id }}">
  <form action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post">
    <label for="VariantSelect-{{ section.id }}">
      {{ 'products.product.product_variants' | t }}
    </label>

    <select id="VariantSelect-{{ section.id }}" data-variant-select>
      {% for variant in product.variants %}
        <option
          value="{{ variant.id }}"
          {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
          {% if variant == product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}selected{% endif %}
        >
          {{ variant.title | escape }}
        </option>
      {% endfor %}
    </select>

    <input
      type="hidden"
      name="id"
      data-cart-variant
      value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
    >

    <button type="submit">{{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}</button>
  </form>
</div>
```

```js
(() => {
  const sectionSelector = '[data-product-picker]';

  function initCompactBuy(root = document) {
    root.querySelectorAll(sectionSelector).forEach((section) => {
      if (section.dataset.compactBuyInitialized === 'true') return;

      const selector = section.querySelector('[data-variant-select]');
      const variantInput = section.querySelector('[data-cart-variant]');
      if (!selector || !variantInput) return;

      selector.addEventListener('change', () => {
        variantInput.value = selector.value;
      });

      section.dataset.compactBuyInitialized = 'true';
    });
  }

  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => initCompactBuy());
  } else {
    initCompactBuy();
  }

  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', (event) => {
    initCompactBuy(event.target);
  });
})();
```

**Why This Patch**

Observed facts:
- The section wrapper already has `data-product-picker` and `data-section-id`.
- The JavaScript currently selects globally instead of within each section instance.
- The label/select ID is static: `VariantSelect`, which creates duplicate IDs when the section appears twice.
- Existing smoke coverage only checked initial load and one available variant.

Inference:
- Scoping queries to each `[data-product-picker]` fixes multiple section instances.
- Listening for `shopify:section:load` fixes Theme Editor section replacement.
- Adding `section.id` to the select ID fixes duplicate label targets and improves accessibility without changing merchant-facing behavior.

Preservation requirements:
- Keep `action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"`.
- Keep `name="id"` on the hidden variant input.
- Keep existing translation keys.
- Keep unavailable variants disabled as currently implemented.
- Do not modify `settings_data.json`, because it has unrelated uncommitted merchant changes.
- Do not change product data, templates, campaigns, live pages, or publish state.

**Tests To Run**

Recommended checks before merge:

1. Product page with two `compact-buy` sections:
   - Change first selector.
   - Confirm first form hidden `name="id"` updates.
   - Confirm second form remains unchanged.
   - Change second selector.
   - Confirm second form hidden `name="id"` updates.

2. Theme Editor:
   - Replace, duplicate, or reload one section.
   - Change its selector.
   - Confirm the new section’s hidden input updates.

3. Accessibility:
   - Confirm each label points to a unique select ID.
   - Keyboard-select variants and submit form.

4. Variant states:
   - Available variant.
   - Disabled unavailable variant remains disabled.
   - Product with only one available variant.

5. Regression:
   - Confirm no duplicate listener behavior after repeated Theme Editor section loads.
   - Confirm standard add-to-cart submission still posts the selected variant ID.

**Unknowns**

Unknown:
- How `compact-buy.js` is loaded.
- Whether the theme has an existing section JavaScript initialization convention that should be used instead.
- Whether subscription/selling-plan products need additional hidden fields.
- Behavior for all-unavailable products is not supplied.
- No browser, Shopify rendering, Theme Editor session, or storefront preview execution is available from the supplied evidence.

**Deployment State**

Status: proposed local patch only.

Not edited, not validated in a browser, not previewed, not uploaded, not published, not live, and not verified on the canonical storefront. Publishing target theme `77102` or changing live theme `77100` requires explicit approval. Rollback would be reverting only the proposed changes to `sections/compact-buy.liquid` and `assets/compact-buy.js`.

